# DEVKIT DESIGN CONSTITUTION

## Premium Apple-Class UI/UX Foundation v1.0

### Global objective

Build an original design system with:

* Apple-level visual refinement
* superior information architecture for complex software
* exceptional mobile, tablet and desktop UX
* precise typography
* sophisticated surface hierarchy
* fluid interaction
* restrained visual language
* high accessibility
* high performance
* semantic design tokens
* consistent behavior across all 3,000 components

Do **not** directly reproduce Apple's proprietary UI, assets, icons, exact layouts, or branded visual elements.

The resulting system should feel:

**calm + premium + precise + fluid + intelligent + beautiful + highly usable.**

---

# 01 — MASTER GRID

Use an **8-point spatial system** as the primary foundation.

### Base unit

```text
1u = 4px
2u = 8px
3u = 12px
4u = 16px
5u = 20px
6u = 24px
8u = 32px
10u = 40px
12u = 48px
14u = 56px
16u = 64px
20u = 80px
24u = 96px
32u = 128px
40u = 160px
48u = 192px
64u = 256px
```

### Allowed spacing tokens

```text
space-0    = 0px
space-1    = 4px
space-2    = 8px
space-3    = 12px
space-4    = 16px
space-5    = 20px
space-6    = 24px
space-8    = 32px
space-10   = 40px
space-12   = 48px
space-14   = 56px
space-16   = 64px
space-20   = 80px
space-24   = 96px
space-32   = 128px
space-40   = 160px
space-48   = 192px
space-64   = 256px
```

**Do not use arbitrary 7px, 11px, 13px, 19px, 27px spacing values.**

Exceptions require explicit component-level justification.

---

# 02 — RESPONSIVE BREAKPOINTS

Use content-driven responsive behavior, but establish these canonical viewport tiers:

```text
Compact       = 0–479px
Mobile        = 480–767px
Tablet        = 768–1023px
Desktop       = 1024–1279px
Large Desktop = 1280–1535px
XL Desktop    = 1536–1919px
Ultra Wide    = 1920px+
```

Do not create separate components for each breakpoint.

One component must adapt across all tiers.

---

# 03 — CONTENT CONTAINERS

Canonical maximum widths:

```text
container-xs       = 480px
container-sm       = 640px
container-md       = 768px
container-lg       = 960px
container-xl       = 1200px
container-2xl      = 1440px
container-3xl      = 1600px
container-full     = 100%
```

### Recommended application max width

```text
Default application content = 1440px
Dashboard                  = 1600px
Data-heavy application     = 1920px
Reading content            = 720px
Forms                      = 640px
Dialog content             = 720px
```

Do not allow ordinary text content to stretch indefinitely across a 1920px screen.

---

# 04 — PAGE PADDING

### Mobile

```text
< 480px  = 16px
480–767  = 20px
```

### Tablet

```text
768–1023px = 24px
```

### Desktop

```text
1024–1279px = 32px
1280–1535px = 40px
1536px+     = 48px
```

For exceptionally dense enterprise interfaces, desktop page padding may reduce to **24px**.

---

# 05 — SECTION SPACING

Use:

```text
tight section      = 24px
normal section     = 32px
large section      = 48px
major section      = 64px
hero section       = 80px
large hero         = 96px
```

Never separate every element with the same amount of space.

---

# 06 — TYPOGRAPHY SCALE

Use a fluid but tokenized typography system.

## Display

```text
Display 1 = 64px / 68px / weight 700
Display 2 = 56px / 60px / weight 700
Display 3 = 48px / 52px / weight 700
```

## Titles

```text
Title 1 = 40px / 48px / weight 700
Title 2 = 32px / 40px / weight 700
Title 3 = 28px / 36px / weight 700
```

## Headings

```text
Heading 1 = 24px / 32px / weight 650
Heading 2 = 20px / 28px / weight 650
Heading 3 = 18px / 24px / weight 650
```

## Body

```text
Body Large  = 17px / 26px / weight 400
Body        = 16px / 24px / weight 400
Body Small  = 14px / 20px / weight 400
```

## Supporting

```text
Label       = 14px / 20px / weight 550
Caption     = 12px / 16px / weight 450
Micro       = 11px / 14px / weight 500
```

## Numeric

```text
Metric XL   = 48px / 52px / weight 700
Metric LG   = 36px / 44px / weight 700
Metric MD   = 28px / 36px / weight 700
Metric SM   = 20px / 28px / weight 650
```

---

# 07 — FONT WEIGHTS

Use only:

```text
Regular       = 400
Medium        = 500
Semibold      = 600
Bold          = 700
Extra Bold    = 800
```

Default body:

```text
400
```

Interactive labels:

```text
500–600
```

Headings:

```text
600–700
```

Hero/display:

```text
700
```

Do not use weight 900 as a normal UI weight.

---

# 08 — FONT FAMILY

Preferred system stack:

```text
-apple-system,
BlinkMacSystemFont,
"SF Pro Display",
"SF Pro Text",
"Segoe UI",
Roboto,
Helvetica,
Arial,
sans-serif
```

For the actual DevKit, use a legally licensed/available font implementation rather than distributing Apple's proprietary fonts without permission.

Use separate optical treatment for:

```text
Display
Text
Numeric
Code
```

---

# 09 — LETTER SPACING

Canonical values:

```text
Display      = -0.03em
Large title  = -0.025em
Title        = -0.02em
Heading      = -0.015em
Body         = 0
Label        = 0
Caption      = +0.01em
Micro        = +0.015em
All caps     = +0.05em
```

Do not use aggressive negative tracking on small text.

---

# 10 — LINE LENGTH

Preferred reading width:

```text
Body text = 45–75 characters per line
Optimal   = approximately 60–68 characters
```

Article/read mode:

```text
600–720px
```

Forms:

```text
480–640px
```

