# 11 — COLOR ARCHITECTURE

Never hardcode component colors.

Use semantic tokens.

## Neutral scale

Define:

```text
Neutral 0
Neutral 50
Neutral 100
Neutral 150
Neutral 200
Neutral 300
Neutral 400
Neutral 500
Neutral 600
Neutral 700
Neutral 800
Neutral 850
Neutral 900
Neutral 950
Neutral 1000
```

The actual RGB values should be defined independently for Light and Dark themes.

---

# 12 — LIGHT THEME SEMANTIC COLORS

Define at minimum:

```text
background.primary
background.secondary
background.tertiary

surface.primary
surface.secondary
surface.tertiary
surface.elevated
surface.floating

text.primary
text.secondary
text.tertiary
text.quaternary
text.disabled
text.inverse

border.subtle
border.default
border.strong

accent.primary
accent.secondary

success
warning
error
info

focus
selection
scrim
```

---

# 13 — COLOR USAGE RATIO

As a default screen-level guideline:

```text
Neutral / background       ≈ 85–92%
Primary text               ≈ 5–10%
Accent + semantic colors   ≈ 2–5%
```

This prevents the application from becoming visually noisy.

Accent color should generally **not occupy more than 10% of the visible interface** unless the design specifically requires it.

---

# 14 — ACCENT COLORS

Define a complete accent scale:

```text
Accent 50
Accent 100
Accent 200
Accent 300
Accent 400
Accent 500
Accent 600
Accent 700
Accent 800
Accent 900
```

Use:

```text
500 = primary visual accent
600 = pressed/emphasis
400 = hover/supporting
100–200 = tinted surfaces
700+ = high-contrast/dark-theme support
```

The exact brand hue should be configurable.

The system must never require one specific brand color.

---

# 15 — SEMANTIC COLORS

Each semantic color receives at least:

```text
background
foreground
border
icon
hover
pressed
```

For:

```text
Success
Warning
Error
Information
```

Never communicate status using color alone.

Add:

```text
icon
text
shape
pattern
or explicit label
```

where necessary.

---

# 16 — DARK MODE

Dark mode gets an independent palette.

Do not mathematically invert Light mode.

Use:

```text
Dark canvas
Dark surface
Dark elevated
Dark floating
Dark overlay
```

with progressively lighter tonal values.

Pure black:

```text
#000000
```

should not be the default application background.

Use true black only where technically or visually justified.

---

# 17 — CONTRAST

Target:

```text
Normal text       ≥ 4.5:1
Large text        ≥ 3:1
UI components     ≥ 3:1
Focus indicator   ≥ 3:1
```

For premium default UI, prefer stronger contrast where it does not compromise the visual hierarchy.

Never sacrifice accessibility for aesthetic subtlety.

---

# 18 — CORNER RADIUS SYSTEM

Canonical radius:

```text
radius-0    = 0px
radius-1    = 4px
radius-2    = 6px
radius-3    = 8px
radius-4    = 10px
radius-5    = 12px
radius-6    = 14px
radius-7    = 16px
radius-8    = 20px
radius-9    = 24px
radius-10   = 28px
radius-full = 9999px
```

### Recommended usage

```text
Micro controls     = 6–8px
Inputs             = 10–12px
Buttons            = 10–14px
Cards              = 16–20px
Large panels       = 20–24px
Dialogs            = 20–24px
Sheets             = 24–28px
Pills              = full
```

Do not automatically use 24px on everything.

---

# 19 — ADAPTIVE RADIUS

Large containers may use:

```text
16px
20px
24px
```

Small controls should generally remain:

```text
8px
10px
12px
14px
```

Nested components should avoid visually conflicting radius scales.

---

# 20 — COMPONENT HEIGHTS

Canonical control heights:

```text
XS = 28px
SM = 32px
MD = 40px
LG = 48px
XL = 56px
```

Default interactive control:

```text
40px
```

Touch-primary control:

```text
48px
```

Large prominent action:

```text
56px
```

---

# 21 — TOUCH TARGETS

Minimum recommended interactive target:

```text
44 × 44px
```

Preferred general target:

```text
48 × 48px
```

Comfortable touch target:

```text
48–56px
```

A visually smaller icon can have an invisible 44–48px hit area.

---

# 22 — ICON SIZES

Canonical:

```text
12px
14px
16px
18px
20px
24px
28px
32px
40px
48px
```

Typical:

```text
Button icon      = 18–20px
Input icon       = 18px
Navigation icon  = 20–24px
Large action     = 24px
Feature icon     = 28–40px
Hero icon        = 40–48px
```

---

# 23 — ICON + TEXT GAP

```text
12px control → 4px gap
14px control → 6px gap
16px control → 8px gap
18–20px icon  → 8px gap
24px icon     → 8–12px gap
```

---

# 24 — BUTTON PADDING

Default:

```text
Horizontal = 16px
Vertical   = 10px
```

Small:

```text
Horizontal = 12px
Vertical   = 6px
```

Large:

```text
Horizontal = 20px
Vertical   = 12px
```

XL:

```text
Horizontal = 24px
Vertical   = 16px
```

Icon-only buttons:

```text
28px
32px
36px
40px
44px
48px
```

with a minimum **44px hit area** for touch.

---

# 25 — CARD PADDING

```text
Compact   = 12px
Small     = 16px
Default   = 20px
Large     = 24px
Hero      = 32px
```

Default card:

```text
padding = 20px
```

Mobile cards:

```text
16px
```

Large desktop feature cards:

```text
24–32px
```

---

# 26 — INPUT PADDING

Default:

```text
horizontal = 12px
vertical   = 10px
```

Large:

```text
horizontal = 16px
vertical   = 12px
```

Icon input:

```text
left/right icon space = 40–44px
```

Do not allow text to collide with icons.

---

# 27 — FORM FIELD GAPS

```text
Label → Input       = 6px
Input → Help text   = 6px
Field → Field       = 16px
Related group       = 24px
Section             = 32px
```

---

# 28 — ELEVATION

Define:

```text
Elevation 0
Elevation 1
Elevation 2
Elevation 3
Elevation 4
Elevation 5
```

Usage:

```text
0 = normal content
1 = cards
2 = floating controls
3 = dropdown/popover
4 = modal/dialog
5 = global overlay
```

Use shadow + tonal contrast together.

Never depend entirely on shadows.

---

# 29 — BORDER WIDTH

Canonical:

```text
subtle = 1px
default = 1px
strong = 1px
emphasis = 2px
```

Avoid 3px+ borders for ordinary UI.

Focus indicators may use:

```text
2px
```

or an external multi-layer focus treatment.

---

# 30 — FOCUS RING

Default:

```text
2px outer focus ring
2px offset
```

For critical accessibility contexts:

```text
2px primary ring
+ 2px contrasting outer separation
```

Never remove focus indicators merely to make the interface visually cleaner.

---

# 31 — MOTION DURATIONS

Canonical:

```text
instant     = 0ms
micro       = 80ms
fast        = 120ms
quick       = 160ms
standard    = 200ms
smooth      = 240ms
medium      = 300ms
large       = 400ms
dramatic    = 500ms
```

Default UI transition:

```text
160–240ms
```

Large modal/sheet:

```text
240–400ms
```

Avoid ordinary UI animations above:

```text
500ms
```

unless there is a strong spatial reason.

---

# 32 — MOTION EASING

Use semantic easing:

```text
ease-standard
ease-emphasized
ease-enter
ease-exit
ease-spring
ease-linear
```

Default:

```text
ease-standard
```

Movement should feel responsive and interruptible.

---

# 33 — SPRING PHYSICS

For draggable/physical interfaces:

```text
stiffness = 300–500
damping   = 25–35
mass      = 0.8–1.2
```

Do not make every component spring.

Spring motion is primarily for:

* sheets
* drag interactions
* floating controls
* physical transitions
* interactive objects

---

# 34 — REDUCED MOTION

When reduced motion is enabled:

```text
complex movement → opacity/crossfade
large transform  → minimal transform
spring           → instant/short transition
parallax         → disabled
decorative motion → disabled
```

Maximum fallback transition:

```text
≤ 120ms
```

---

# 35 — BLUR / MATERIAL

Canonical blur levels:

```text
blur-sm = 8px
blur-md = 16px
blur-lg = 24px
blur-xl = 32px
blur-2xl = 48px
```

Use primarily for:

* floating navigation
* overlays
* sheets
* popovers
* contextual surfaces

Never use blur merely because it looks fashionable.

---

# 36 — OPACITY

Canonical:

```text
0%
5%
8%
10%
12%
16%
24%
32%
50%
64%
80%
90%
100%
```

Use semantic tokens.

Examples:

```text
disabled ≈ 50–60%
scrim     ≈ 40–60%
secondary ≈ 70–80%
```

Do not use opacity to make text inaccessible.

---

# 37 — OVERLAY SCRIM

Default:

```text
40–50%
```

Heavy modal:

```text
50–60%
```

Light contextual overlay:

```text
20–32%
```

The scrim should preserve enough contextual awareness without distracting from the active surface.

---

# 38 — Z-INDEX

Use semantic layers:

```text
base             = 0
raised           = 10
sticky           = 100
navigation       = 200
floating         = 300
dropdown         = 400
popover          = 500
tooltip          = 600
drawer           = 700
modal            = 800
critical         = 900
system           = 1000
```

No component may arbitrarily use:

```text
999999
```

---

# 39 — GRID

Use:

```text
4-column mobile
8-column tablet
12-column desktop
12-column large desktop
```

Typical desktop gap:

```text
24px
```

Tablet:

```text
20px
```

Mobile:

```text
16px
```

---

# 40 — COMPONENT GAP SYSTEM

Use:

```text
4px   = icon/metadata relationship
8px   = tightly related elements
12px  = control relationships
16px  = standard element relationship
24px  = group relationship
32px  = section relationship
48px  = major section
64px+ = page-level separation
```

---

# 41 — DATA DENSITY

Three global modes:

### Compact

```text
Control height = 32px
Row height     = 36px
Padding        = 8–12px
```

### Comfortable

```text
Control height = 40px
Row height     = 44px
Padding        = 12–16px
```

### Spacious

```text
Control height = 48px
Row height     = 52–56px
Padding        = 16–20px
```

Default:

**Comfortable.**

---

# 42 — TABLE ROWS

Default:

```text
44px
```

Compact:

```text
36px
```

Spacious:

```text
52px
```

Mobile tables should transform into cards or responsive rows when horizontal compression harms usability.

---

# 43 — NAVIGATION HEIGHT

Desktop primary navigation:

```text
56px
```

Large navigation:

```text
64px
```

Mobile top navigation:

```text
56px
```

Mobile bottom navigation:

```text
64–80px
```

Include safe-area padding where applicable.

---

